{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>And a spirit of jealousy passes over him.</b> A spirit of purity to investigate her, since he knows she has deviated from the ways of modesty." "<b>And he becomes jealous of his wife.</b> He warns her and says: Do not seclude yourself with a certain man." "<b>Or a spirit of jealousy passes over him.</b> A spirit of groundless folly, without cause that warrants jealousy." "<b>And she has not defiled herself.</b> But if she transgressed his warning and secluded herself, even so."], :book :numbers, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 5, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:38:36.402897231Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}